                <pb facs="0475" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711F.1914/403: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-24T10:00:00-05:00">December 24, 1941—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:57 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>539. Reference my letter to the Under Secretary of December 4<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d367-f1"/> reporting conversation with the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs regarding the 12 points. Yesterday afternoon the Minister said to me the
                    following: The President is greatly concerned over the delay in completing the
                    negotiations on the 12 points and the lease contract and feels his Government is
                    being criticized here because of the delay. He had hoped to make progress before
                    this but the illness of the Panamanian Ambassador at Washington has prevented
                    it. He appreciates that it was agreed that negotiations on the 12 points would
                    take place in Washington but in view of the Ambassador’s illness the President
                    now asks that I transmit to the State Department the following request: That the
                    United States Government agrees now that simultaneously with reaching agreement
                    on the lease contract the United States Government will by executive action,
                    without necessity of awaiting action by Congress, turn the railroad lots over to
                    Panama and liquidate the credit for the Rio Hato Highway.</p>
                <p>Please instruct.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
